{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HZy5KFwoMEfxsW8mGRkjLc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '完全 reframe 为 diagnostic/analysis paper。Title: \"Dissecting Credit\n2\t  Assignment Failure in Multi-Turn LLM Agent RL: A Dual-Mechanism Analysis\"。 核心叙事：episode-level\n3\t  是 necessary but not sufficient，消除 window-level 问题后暴露更深层 credit assignment 瓶颈。 GAE\n4\t  >> episode-level GRPO 证明 per-token credit 是关键缺失。Sign misattribution 是主要但非唯一因素——entropy\n5\t  collapse、KL drift、information loss 共同作用。 贡献定位为 failure mode taxonomy + actionable\n6\t  guidelines + cross-framework design analysis。 Selective verification 完全移入 future\n7\t  work。Claim 2/3 删除。\n8\t\n9\t  '\n10\timagined_experiments:\n11\t- name: Episode-level GRPO convergence (exp029 continuation)\n12\t  plan_id: plan_001\n13\t  description: Episode-level GRPO 继续训练至 step 50+，观察是否突破 28% plateau\n14\t  expected_results:\n15\t    step15_val_success: 0.28125\n16\t    step20_val_success: 0.27\n17\t    step30_val_success: 0.26\n18\t    step40_val_success: 0.25\n19\t    step50_val_success: 0.24\n20\t    convergence_val_success: 0.25\n21\t    step50_train_success: 0.5\n22\t    step50_train_pass_at_8: 0.8125\n23\t    step50_val_pass_at_1: 0.25\n24\t    step50_val_pass_at_8: 0.94\n25\t    step50_val_action_is_valid: 0.58\n26\t    step50_entropy: 0.12\n27\t    step50_ppo_kl: 0.015\n28\t    train_val_gap_pp: 25\n29\t    plateau_onset_step: 10\n30\t    plateau_duration_steps: 40\n31\t  result_rationale: 'Episode-level GRPO 在 step 10 后进入 plateau（25-28%），训练 success 持续上升至\n32\t    ~50% 但 val 不跟随—— 经典 overfitting to training distribution。根因：GRPO 的 bandit-style\n33\t    credit assignment（所有 token 共享同一 advantage） 无法学习 per-step 策略改进。模型学会了 \"在训练任务分布上做对的\n34\t    trajectory pattern\"，但缺乏 fine-grained credit 来泛化到 unseen task instance。Entropy\n35\t    持续下降表明 policy 在 narrowing 但未在 improving。 pass@8=0.94 证明 policy 有能力但 greedy decoding\n36\t    无法稳定触发正确路径——credit assignment 不够精细， 无法可靠地将 probability mass 集中到 correct action\n37\t    sequence 上。\n38\t\n39\t    '\n40\t  tables:\n41\t  - name: Convergence trajectory\n42\t    columns:\n43\t    - step\n44\t    - val_success\n45\t    - train_success\n46\t    - val_pass@8\n47\t    - entropy\n48\t    - kl\n49\t    rows:\n50\t    - - 5\n51\t      - 0.25\n52\t      - 0.31\n53\t      - 0.88\n54\t      - 0.2\n55\t      - 0.003\n56\t    - - 10\n57\t      - 0.25\n58\t      - 0.38\n59\t      - 0.91\n60\t      - 0.17\n61\t      - 0.007\n62\t    - - 15\n63\t      - 0.28\n64\t      - 0.44\n65\t      - 0.93\n66\t      - 0.15\n67\t      - 0.01\n68\t    - - 20\n69\t      - 0.27\n70\t      - 0.47\n71\t      - 0.93\n72\t      - 0.14\n73\t      - 0.012\n74\t    - - 30\n75\t      - 0.26\n76\t      - 0.5\n77\t      - 0.94\n78\t      - 0.13\n79\t      - 0.014\n80\t    - - 40\n81\t      - 0.25\n82\t      - 0.5\n83\t      - 0.94\n84\t      - 0.12\n85\t      - 0.015\n86\t    - - 50\n87\t      - 0.24\n88\t      - 0.5\n89\t      - 0.94\n90\t      - 0.12\n91\t      - 0.015\n92\t  figures_description:\n93\t  - 'Learning curve: val_success plateau at 25-28% from step 10 onward, train_success\n94\t    diverging upward to 50%. Classic overfitting gap.'\n95\t  - 'Entropy decay curve: monotonic decrease from 0.25 → 0.12, policy narrows without\n96\t    improving generalization.'\n97\t  analysis: 'Plateau 确认 episode-level GRPO 的根本限制：bandit-style advantage 足以消除 sign\n98\t    misattribution， 但不足以提供 per-token credit assignment。25-28% 是 \"episode-level 能做到的天花板\"\n99\t    在当前 reward density 下。 这是 analysis paper 的核心发现之一：episode-level 解决了 step-independent\n100\t    的问题但暴露了更深层瓶颈。\n101\t\n102\t    '\n103\t- name: Context window h-sweep ablation (3 seeds each)\n104\t  plan_id: plan_002\n105\t  description: h={2, 5, 10, 20, full} sweep，每个 3 seeds，15 steps each\n106\t  expected_results:\n107\t    h2_seed1_step15_success: 0.0\n108\t    h2_seed2_step15_success: 0.03\n109\t    h2_seed3_step15_success: 0.0\n110\t    h2_mean: 0.01\n111\t    h2_std: 0.017\n112\t    h2_collapse_step_mean: 4.3\n113\t    h5_seed1_step15_success: 0.06\n114\t    h5_seed2_step15_success: 0.0\n115\t    h5_seed3_step15_success: 0.09\n116\t    h5_mean: 0.05\n117\t    h5_std: 0.046\n118\t    h5_collapse_rate: 0.33\n119\t    h10_seed1_step15_success: 0.12\n120\t    h10_seed2_step15_success: 0.03\n121\t    h10_seed3_step15_success: 0.16\n122\t    h10_mean: 0.103\n123\t    h10_std: 0.066\n124\t    h20_seed1_step15_success: 0.19\n125\t    h20_seed2_step15_success: 0.09\n126\t    h20_seed3_step15_success: 0.22\n127\t    h20_mean: 0.167\n128\t    h20_std: 0.068\n129\t    full_seed1_step15_success: 0.28\n130\t    full_seed2_step15_success: 0.19\n131\t    full_seed3_step15_success: 0.25\n132\t    full_mean: 0.24\n133\t    full_std: 0.046\n134\t    monotonic_ordering_violated: true\n135\t    h5_occasionally_beats_h10: true\n136\t    h20_occasionally_collapses: true\n137\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档的关键特征：h-sweep 不是 clean monotonic function。h=2 一致崩溃（sign\n138\t    misattribution + extreme information loss）， 但 h=5 和 h=10 之间、h=10 和 h=20 之间存在 seed\n139\t    间交叉——某些 seed 下 h=5 偶尔优于 h=10， h=20 偶尔 collapse。这说明 cliff 位置依赖于 random initialization\n140\t    和 early training dynamics， 而非仅由 h 值决定。高 cross-seed variance 削弱了 \"clean cliff at\n141\t    h=10\" 的叙事， 但仍支持 \"smaller h systematically worse on average\" 的趋势。Non-monotonicity\n142\t    来自 不同 seed 的 entropy dynamics 差异：某些 seed 早期 exploration 更好，偶尔让 h=5 找到可行策略。\n143\t\n144\t    '\n145\t  tables:\n146\t  - name: h-sweep summary (step 15, 3 seeds)\n147\t    columns:\n148\t    - h\n149\t    - seed1\n150\t    - seed2\n151\t    - seed3\n152\t    - mean\n153\t    - std\n154\t    - collapse_rate\n155\t    rows:\n156\t    - - h=2\n157\t      - 0.0\n158\t      - 0.03\n159\t      - 0.0\n160\t      - 0.01\n161\t      - 0.017\n162\t      - 3/3\n163\t    - - h=5\n164\t      - 0.06\n165\t      - 0.0\n166\t      - 0.09\n167\t      - 0.05\n168\t      - 0.046\n169\t      - 1/3\n170\t    - - h=10\n171\t      - 0.12\n172\t      - 0.03\n173\t      - 0.16\n174\t      - 0.103\n175\t      - 0.066\n176\t      - 0/3\n177\t    - - h=20\n178\t      - 0.19\n179\t      - 0.09\n180\t      - 0.22\n181\t      - 0.167\n182\t      - 0.068\n183\t      - 0/3\n184\t    - - full\n185\t      - 0.28\n186\t      - 0.19\n187\t      - 0.25\n188\t      - 0.24\n189\t      - 0.046\n190\t      - 0/3\n191\t  figures_description:\n192\t  - 'Box plot: h vs val_success with individual seed points. Trend is upward but boxes\n193\t    overlap between adjacent h values. Error bars large.'\n194\t  - 'Collapse timeline: h=2 collapses by step 4-5 across all seeds; h=5 collapses\n195\t    in 1/3 seeds; h≥10 no full collapse but h=20 seed2 shows temporary dip.'\n196\t  analysis: 'Non-monotonic 结果对 paper 是挑战也是机会。不能 claim \"clean cliff\"，但可以 reframe 为\n197\t    \"credit assignment failure is a stochastic phenomenon whose probability increases\n198\t    with smaller h\"—— 这更符合 analysis paper 的 tone。Cross-seed variance 本身是 failure mode\n199\t    taxonomy 的一条： \"training instability as a function of context window\" 是独立 failure\n200\t    mechanism。 需要从 \"threshold effect\" 叙事转向 \"probabilistic degradation\" 叙事。\n201\t\n202\t    '\n203\t- name: Multi-seed replication (5 seeds)\n204\t  plan_id: plan_003\n205\t  description: Episode-level GRPO 5 seeds（含 exp029 原始 seed），report mean ± std\n206\t  expected_results:\n207\t    seed1_val_success: 0.28\n208\t    seed2_val_success: 0.19\n209\t    seed3_val_success: 0.25\n210\t    seed4_val_success: 0.15\n211\t    seed5_val_success: 0.3\n212\t    mean_val_success: 0.234\n213\t    std_val_success: 0.062\n214\t    std_pp: 6.2\n215\t    min_val_success: 0.15\n216\t    max_val_success: 0.3\n217\t    range_pp: 15\n218\t    seeds_above_25pct: 3\n219\t    seeds_below_20pct: 1\n220\t    mean_train_success: 0.46\n221\t    train_val_gap_mean_pp: 22.6\n222\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档要求 std > 7pp。这里 std=6.2pp 接近但略低于 7pp 边界——真实的 worst 场景中\n223\t    5 seeds 可能落在 6-9pp 范围。 关键问题：seed4 只达到 15%（接近 step-independent 水平），说明 episode-level\n224\t    的优势在某些 seed 下大幅削弱。 这源于 GRPO 的 group normalization 对初始 rollout 分布敏感——如果前几步 rollout\n225\t    恰好全部失败， advantage 全为 0（无 variance），模型无法获得有效梯度。Seed4 可能经历了 \"cold start\" 问题： 早期\n226\t    rollout 全败 → advantage=0 → 无学习 → 持续全败的恶性循环。高 variance 使 95% CI 覆盖 0， 削弱了 episode-level\n227\t    作为 \"solution\" 的 claim，但强化了 analysis paper 的叙事—— \"即使 episode-level 也不稳定，RL for\n228\t    LLM agents 需要更根本性的改进\"。\n229\t\n230\t    '\n231\t  tables:\n232\t  - name: Multi-seed results (step 15 checkpoint)\n233\t    columns:\n234\t    - seed\n235\t    - val_success\n236\t    - train_success\n237\t    - action_is_valid\n238\t    - plateau_step\n239\t    rows:\n240\t    - - 1\n241\t      - 0.28\n242\t      - 0.44\n243\t      - 0.55\n244\t      - 10\n245\t    - - 2\n246\t      - 0.19\n247\t      - 0.41\n248\t      - 0.52\n249\t      - 8\n250\t    - - 3\n251\t      - 0.25\n252\t      - 0.47\n253\t      - 0.56\n254\t      - 10\n255\t    - - 4\n256\t      - 0.15\n257\t      - 0.35\n258\t      - 0.48\n259\t      - 12\n260\t    - - 5\n261\t      - 0.3\n262\t      - 0.5\n263\t      - 0.58\n264\t      - 10\n265\t  - name: Summary statistics\n266\t    columns:\n267\t    - metric\n268\t    - mean\n269\t    - std\n270\t    - 95% CI\n271\t    rows:\n272\t    - - val_success\n273\t      - 0.234\n274\t      - 0.062\n275\t      - '[0.157, 0.311]'\n276\t    - - train_success\n277\t      - 0.434\n278\t      - 0.057\n279\t      - '[0.363, 0.505]'\n280\t    - - action_is_valid\n281\t      - 0.538\n282\t      - 0.038\n283\t      - '[0.491, 0.585]'\n284\t  figures_description:\n285\t  - Swarm plot with mean ± 95% CI. CI is wide (15.7pp-31.1%), overlaps with step-independent\n286\t    range for low seeds.\n287\t  analysis: '95% CI [15.7%, 31.1%] 太宽，无法 credibly claim episode-level \"solves\" the\n288\t    problem。 但 mean 仍显著高于 step-independent mean（~2%），所以 \"episode-level helps but doesn''t\n289\t    solve\" 是可靠 claim。 Analysis paper framing: 这证明了 credit assignment 问题的多层性——episode-level\n290\t    消除了 sign misattribution 但暴露了 GRPO 的 cold-start sensitivity 和 bandit-level credit\n291\t    的根本限制。\n292\t\n293\t    '\n294\t- name: GAE baseline comparison\n295\t  plan_id: plan_003b\n296\t  description: GAE(λ=0.95) 和 GAE(λ=1.0, γ=1.0) baselines，15 steps × 3 seeds\n297\t  expected_results:\n298\t    gae_095_seed1_success: 0.44\n299\t    gae_095_seed2_success: 0.38\n300\t    gae_095_seed3_success: 0.41\n301\t    gae_095_mean: 0.41\n302\t    gae_095_std: 0.03\n303\t    gae_10_10_seed1_success: 0.37\n304\t    gae_10_10_seed2_success: 0.34\n305\t    gae_10_10_seed3_success: 0.39\n306\t    gae_10_10_mean: 0.367\n307\t    gae_10_10_std: 0.025\n308\t    episode_grpo_mean: 0.234\n309\t    gae_095_vs_episode_delta_pp: 17.6\n310\t    gae_10_vs_episode_delta_pp: 13.3\n311\t    gae_095_per_token_adv_variance: 0.42\n312\t    episode_grpo_per_token_adv_variance: 0.0\n313\t    step_independent_mean: 0.02\n314\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档要求 GAE >> episode-level GRPO（delta > 15pp）。GAE(λ=0.95)\n315\t    达到 41%—— 因为 critic 提供 per-token temporal difference signal，每个 action 获得独立的 advantage\n316\t    estimate， 而非 GRPO 的 \"全 trajectory 同一 advantage\"。这是 worst 档的核心发现： episode-level\n317\t    GRPO 的 plateau 不是 episode-level 本身的问题，而是 GRPO 的 bandit-style credit 的问题。 GAE 通过\n318\t    value function 提供 fine-grained credit，打破了 plateau。 GAE(λ=1,γ=1) 略低于 GAE(0.95)，因为无\n319\t    discount 导致 variance 更高。 Delta=17.6pp 直接证明：per-token credit assignment 是关键缺失，episode-level\n320\t    只是 necessary condition。 这彻底改变 paper story——从 \"episode-level solves it\" 到 \"episode-level\n321\t    is necessary but per-token credit is the real bottleneck\"。\n322\t\n323\t    '\n324\t  tables:\n325\t  - name: Method comparison (step 15)\n326\t    columns:\n327\t    - method\n328\t    - seed1\n329\t    - seed2\n330\t    - seed3\n331\t    - mean\n332\t    - std\n333\t    rows:\n334\t    - - step-independent (h=2)\n335\t      - 0.0\n336\t      - 0.03\n337\t      - 0.0\n338\t      - 0.01\n339\t      - 0.017\n340\t    - - episode-level GRPO\n341\t      - 0.28\n342\t      - 0.19\n343\t      - 0.25\n344\t      - 0.24\n345\t      - 0.046\n346\t    - - GAE(λ=1,γ=1)\n347\t      - 0.37\n348\t      - 0.34\n349\t      - 0.39\n350\t      - 0.367\n351\t      - 0.025\n352\t    - - GAE(λ=0.95,γ=1)\n353\t      - 0.44\n354\t      - 0.38\n355\t      - 0.41\n356\t      - 0.41\n357\t      - 0.03\n358\t  figures_description:\n359\t  - 'Bar chart: 4 methods with error bars. Clear staircase: step-ind << episode-GRPO\n360\t    << GAE(1,1) < GAE(0.95). Gap between GRPO and GAE is the paper''s key diagnostic\n361\t    finding.'\n362\t  analysis: 'GAE 的大幅领先是 analysis paper 的最强证据：问题不只是 window-level vs episode-level，\n363\t    而是 credit granularity 的 spectrum。GRPO episode-level 在 spectrum 中间（消除了 sign error\n364\t    但无 per-token credit）， GAE 在另一端（full per-token credit via value function）。这支持 failure\n365\t    mode taxonomy 的第三种机制： \"bandit-level credit insufficiency\"——即使 advantage 方向正确，所有\n366\t    token 共享同一 magnitude 也无法 区分 trajectory 中的关键决策点和无关步骤。\n367\t\n368\t    '\n369\t- name: Episode-level + valid_action_bonus\n370\t  plan_id: plan_003c\n371\t  description: Episode-level + valid_action_bonus=0.05，测试是否安全突破 plateau\n372\t  expected_results:\n373\t    step15_val_success: 0.22\n374\t    step15_val_action_is_valid: 0.72\n375\t    step15_train_success: 0.39\n376\t    valid_bonus_vs_task_ratio: 0.35\n377\t    gaming_detected: false\n378\t    success_improvement_vs_baseline: -0.06\n379\t    action_is_valid_improvement_pp: 17\n380\t    reward_composition_valid_pct: 0.28\n381\t    reward_composition_task_pct: 0.72\n382\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 valid_action_bonus 在 episode-level 中不 game（因为模型优化整条\n383\t    trajectory total reward）， action_is_valid 确实从 55% 提升到 72%，但 success 反而略降（22% <\n384\t    28%）。 原因：valid_action_bonus 改变了 reward landscape，使模型偏向 \"safe but ineffective\"\n385\t    actions—— valid 但不 goal-directed 的 action（如反复 examine 已知物体）获得持续正 reward， 而 risky\n386\t    but potentially successful 的 exploration 策略被抑制。Episode-level 下不存在 per-step gaming，\n387\t    但 dense bonus 仍扭曲了 trajectory-level 的 learning signal——模型学会生成 \"很多 valid action\n388\t    的长 trajectory\" 而非 \"goal-directed 的短 trajectory\"。这是 analysis paper 的另一个 insight：\n389\t    dense reward 在 episode-level 下的失效模式与 step-independent 不同但同样有害。\n390\t\n391\t    '\n392\t  tables:\n393\t  - name: valid_action_bonus ablation\n394\t    columns:\n395\t    - config\n396\t    - val_success\n397\t    - action_is_valid\n398\t    - avg_trajectory_len\n399\t    - reward_mean\n400\t    rows:\n401\t    - - episode-level (baseline)\n402\t      - 0.28\n403\t      - 0.55\n404\t      - 38.2\n405\t      - 2.81\n406\t    - - episode-level + bonus=0.05\n407\t      - 0.22\n408\t      - 0.72\n409\t      - 45.6\n410\t      - 3.92\n411\t  figures_description:\n412\t  - 'Dual-axis plot: action_is_valid improves (good) but success drops (bad). Trajectory\n413\t    length increases — model generates more valid-but-aimless steps.'\n414\t  analysis: 'valid_action_bonus 未引入 step-independent 式 gaming，但通过 reward shaping 偏移了\n415\t    policy gradient direction。 这是 failure mode taxonomy 的第四种机制：\"reward misalignment\n416\t    under sparse task signal\"—— 当 task reward 稀疏且 episode-level credit 粗糙时，任何 dense\n417\t    auxiliary reward 都容易主导 learning。 进一步证明 per-token credit（如 GAE）才是根本解。\n418\t\n419\t    '\n420\t- name: Credit assignment mechanism empirical verification\n421\t  plan_id: plan_004\n422\t  description: Per-window advantage logging，验证 sign misattribution 机制\n423\t  expected_results:\n424\t    sign_vs_outcome_correlation: 0.73\n425\t    sign_vs_local_quality_correlation: 0.28\n426\t    magnitude_position_decay_r2: 0.61\n427\t    episode_level_adv_variance: 0.0\n428\t    success_episodes_all_positive_pct: 0.78\n429\t    failure_episodes_all_negative_pct: 0.82\n430\t    mixed_sign_episodes_pct: 0.2\n431\t    gamma_k_decay_slope: -0.032\n432\t    confound_kl_correlation: 0.31\n433\t    confound_entropy_correlation: 0.27\n434\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档的关键：sign-outcome correlation 只有 0.73（而非预期的 >0.95），sign-local_quality\n435\t    correlation 达到 0.28（而非预期的 ~0）。这意味着 sign misattribution 存在但有显著混杂因素。 Correlation\n436\t    < 1.0 的原因：GRPO 的 group normalization 使得同一 group 内的 advantage 不完全由 episode outcome\n437\t    决定—— 如果 group 内所有 episode 都成功（或都失败），normalization 后 advantage 反映 relative 差异而非\n438\t    absolute 成败。 这在成功率较高的 training episodes 中尤为明显。 Local quality correlation = 0.28\n439\t    的原因：window-local action quality 与 episode success 本身存在弱正相关 （好的 local action 确实\n440\t    contribute to success），所以 sign-local 相关性部分反映了 genuine causal path 而非纯 misattribution。这是混杂因素：无法将\n441\t    sign-local 相关性 100% 归因于 misattribution， 因为部分是 legitimate credit signal。 KL divergence\n442\t    和 entropy 也与 advantage sign 相关（r=0.31, 0.27），说明 policy drift 和 exploration dynamics\n443\t    独立影响 advantage distribution。\n444\t\n445\t    '\n446\t  tables:\n447\t  - name: Mechanism verification (h=2, seed 2, step 5)\n448\t    columns:\n449\t    - metric\n450\t    - observed\n451\t    - hypothesis\n452\t    - status\n453\t    rows:\n454\t    - - sign-outcome corr\n455\t      - 0.73\n456\t      - '>0.95'\n457\t      - PARTIAL — significant confounds\n458\t    - - sign-local_quality corr\n459\t      - 0.28\n460\t      - <0.1\n461\t      - FAILED — non-negligible correlation\n462\t    - - magnitude decay R²\n463\t      - 0.61\n464\t      - '>0.85'\n465\t      - PARTIAL — decay exists but noisy\n466\t    - - episode-level adv variance\n467\t      - 0.0\n468\t      - '0.0'\n469\t      - CONFIRMED\n470\t    - - '% success eps all-positive'\n471\t      - 78%\n472\t      - '>95%'\n473\t      - PARTIAL — 22% have mixed signs\n474\t  - name: Confound analysis\n475\t    columns:\n476\t    - confound_variable\n477\t    - correlation_with_adv_sign\n478\t    - p_value\n479\t    rows:\n480\t    - - episode_outcome\n481\t      - 0.73\n482\t      - <0.001\n483\t    - - local_action_quality\n484\t      - 0.28\n485\t      - <0.01\n486\t    - - KL_divergence\n487\t      - 0.31\n488\t      - <0.01\n489\t    - - entropy\n490\t      - 0.27\n491\t      - <0.01\n492\t    - - window_position\n493\t      - -0.18\n494\t      - <0.05\n495\t  figures_description:\n496\t  - 'Scatter: advantage sign vs episode outcome (color=local quality). Not the clean\n497\t    binary separation expected — significant overlap region.'\n498\t  - 'Partial correlation decomposition: pie chart showing episode outcome explains\n499\t    53%, local quality 16%, KL 10%, entropy 8%, unexplained 13%.'\n500\t  analysis: 'Sign misattribution 存在但不是 sole mechanism——这是 worst 档的核心困难。不能 claim \"advantage\n501\t    sign is entirely determined by episode outcome\"。 需要 reframe 为 \"sign misattribution\n502\t    is the dominant but not sole factor in credit assignment failure\"。 混杂因素（KL drift、entropy\n503\t    dynamics）本身成为 failure mode taxonomy 的独立条目。 Partial correlation decomposition 成为\n504\t    analysis paper 的关键贡献：量化每种机制对 credit assignment failure 的贡献占比。\n505\t\n506\t    '\n507\t- name: Action-change statistics from always-on runs\n508\t  plan_id: plan_005\n509\t  description: 从 exp029 checkpoint 收集 action-change 统计\n510\t  expected_results:\n511\t    action_change_rate: 0.18\n512\t    confirmatory_rate: 0.82\n513\t    action_change_success_correlation: 0.08\n514\t    action_change_success_p_value: 0.12\n515\t    per_task_action_change_std: 0.09\n516\t    pick_action_change_rate: 0.12\n517\t    clean_action_change_rate: 0.22\n518\t    heat_action_change_rate: 0.2\n519\t    cool_action_change_rate: 0.15\n520\t    examine_action_change_rate: 0.25\n521\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 action-change-success correlation 仅 0.08 且 p=0.12（不显著）。\n522\t    原因：episode-level model 只有 25% success rate，样本中 successful episodes 太少导致 statistical\n523\t    power 不足。 更根本的问题：在 25% success 的 agent 上，action change 基本是 noise—— model 的 verification\n524\t    输出质量太低，无论是否 change action 都可能是随机的。 Confirmatory rate 82% 符合预期（大部分 verification\n525\t    不改变行为）， 但这也意味着 action change 事件太稀疏（只有 18%），与 success 的 correlation 在统计上不可靠。 这直接阻碍了\n526\t    Phase B：如果 action change 不是 success 的有效 signal， 用它作 intrinsic reward 没有理论基础。\n527\t\n528\t    '\n529\t  tables:\n530\t  - name: Action-change statistics\n531\t    columns:\n532\t    - metric\n533\t    - value\n534\t    rows:\n535\t    - - overall action change rate\n536\t      - 18%\n537\t    - - confirmatory rate\n538\t      - 82%\n539\t    - - action_change-success correlation\n540\t      - r=0.08, p=0.12\n541\t    - - N (episodes)\n542\t      - 128\n543\t    - - N (verification events)\n544\t      - 2304\n545\t    - - N (action changes)\n546\t      - 415\n547\t  figures_description:\n548\t  - 'Contingency table heatmap: action_change × episode_success. No clear pattern\n549\t    — action change is roughly equally distributed across success/failure episodes.'\n550\t  analysis: 'Action change 作为 intrinsic reward 缺乏 empirical grounding。在 worst 档下，\n551\t    这个结果直接导致 Claim 2 无法成立——selective verification 失去了 reward signal。 Analysis paper\n552\t    中可以作为 \"why selective verification is hard for weak agents\" 的一个 finding。\n553\t\n554\t    '\n555\t- name: Selective verification implementation\n556\t  plan_id: plan_006\n557\t  description: Code-only：实现 binary verify/skip decision\n558\t  expected_results:\n559\t    implementation_status: completed\n560\t    code_changes_files: 4\n561\t    gpu_hours: 0\n562\t  result_rationale: '纯代码实现，不依赖实验结果。在 worst 档下仍可完成，但后续使用这个 implementation 的实验效果差。\n563\t\n564\t    '\n565\t  tables: []\n566\t  figures_description: []\n567\t  analysis: 'Implementation 本身无 worst 档问题。但 plan_005 的 weak correlation 预示 plan_007\n568\t    会失败。\n569\t\n570\t    '\n571\t- name: B-IAVR selective verification training\n572\t  plan_id: plan_007\n573\t  description: 用 action-change reward 训练 selective verification policy\n574\t  expected_results:\n575\t    verification_rate_reduction_pct: 12\n576\t    val_success: 0.16\n577\t    baseline_always_on_success: 0.25\n578\t    success_delta_pp: -9\n579\t    training_converged: false\n580\t    reward_signal_informative: false\n581\t    verification_rate: 0.88\n582\t    policy_learned_skip: false\n583\t    training_steps_before_abort: 20\n584\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：selective verification 无法 deliver clear win。两个根因叠加： (1)\n585\t    plan_005 显示 action-change 不是有效 signal（r=0.08, p=0.12），用它做 reward 等于训练 on noise；\n586\t    (2) base agent 只有 25% success，skip verification 直接降低 performance 且模型无法学会 when\n587\t    to skip。 Verification rate 只降了 12%（模型几乎总是 verify），因为 skip 的 penalty（success 下降）远大于\n588\t    action-change reward 的 bonus。Policy 本质上退化为 \"always verify\"—— 因为在 25% success 的\n589\t    agent 上，任何 skip 都有显著 performance cost。 Success 降至 16%（比 baseline 低 9pp），因为即使少量的\n590\t    skip 也损害了 performance。\n591\t\n592\t    '\n593\t  tables:\n594\t  - name: B-IAVR results\n595\t    columns:\n596\t    - policy\n597\t    - val_success\n598\t    - verification_rate\n599\t    - cost_reduction\n600\t    rows:\n601\t    - - always-on\n602\t      - 0.25\n603\t      - 100%\n604\t      - 0%\n605\t    - - B-IAVR (learned)\n606\t      - 0.16\n607\t      - 88%\n608\t      - 12%\n609\t    - - random-50%\n610\t      - 0.14\n611\t      - 50%\n612\t      - 50%\n613\t    - - no-verify\n614\t      - 0.13\n615\t      - 0%\n616\t      - 100%\n617\t  figures_description:\n618\t  - 'Pareto frontier: success vs cost. B-IAVR barely separates from always-on, nowhere\n619\t    near efficient frontier.'\n620\t  analysis: 'Selective verification 在 worst 档下完全无法作为 paper contribution。 必须移入 future\n621\t    work，framed as \"requires stronger base agent + better reward signal\"。\n622\t\n623\t    '\n624\t- name: Selective verification full comparison\n625\t  plan_id: plan_008\n626\t  description: Always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence 对比\n627\t  expected_results:\n628\t    always_on_success: 0.25\n629\t    always_on_verify_rate: 1.0\n630\t    biavr_success: 0.16\n631\t    biavr_verify_rate: 0.88\n632\t    no_verify_success: 0.13\n633\t    no_verify_rate: 0.0\n634\t    random_50_success: 0.14\n635\t    random_50_rate: 0.5\n636\t    confidence_success: 0.19\n637\t    confidence_verify_rate: 0.65\n638\t    biavr_dominates_pareto: false\n639\t    best_cost_performance: confidence-threshold\n640\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：B-IAVR 不 dominate Pareto frontier。Confidence-based baseline\n641\t    意外优于 B-IAVR—— 因为 confidence threshold 是 model-intrinsic signal（policy entropy），\n642\t    比 action-change 这个 noisy extrinsic signal 更 informative。 Confidence 方法在 entropy\n643\t    高时 verify（不确定时检查），在 entropy 低时 skip（确定时省略）， 这 naturally 对齐 \"verification is useful\n644\t    when uncertain\"。 B-IAVR 学到的 policy 没有这种 alignment 因为 training signal 太弱。 所有 selective\n645\t    方法都比 always-on 差（delta > 5pp），因为 base agent 太弱—— verification 在 25% agent 上几乎总是有用的（因为\n646\t    agent 经常犯错）。\n647\t\n648\t    '\n649\t  tables:\n650\t  - name: Full comparison (step 15 checkpoint, 128 val episodes)\n651\t    columns:\n652\t    - method\n653\t    - success\n654\t    - verify_rate\n655\t    - total_tokens\n656\t    - success_per_token\n657\t    rows:\n658\t    - - always-on\n659\t      - 25.0%\n660\t      - 100%\n661\t      - 1.0x\n662\t      - '0.250'\n663\t    - - confidence-0.5\n664\t      - 19.0%\n665\t      - 65%\n666\t      - 0.72x\n667\t      - '0.264'\n668\t    - - B-IAVR\n669\t      - 16.0%\n670\t      - 88%\n671\t      - 0.93x\n672\t      - '0.172'\n673\t    - - random-50%\n674\t      - 14.0%\n675\t      - 50%\n676\t      - 0.62x\n677\t      - '0.226'\n678\t    - - no-verify\n679\t      - 13.0%\n680\t      - 0%\n681\t      - 0.45x\n682\t      - '0.289'\n683\t  figures_description:\n684\t  - 'Pareto frontier plot: no-verify has best token-efficiency (trivially), confidence-threshold\n685\t    dominates B-IAVR. B-IAVR is dominated — not on the frontier.'\n686\t  analysis: 'B-IAVR 被 confidence baseline dominate，这对 Claim 3 是致命的。 但 analysis paper\n687\t    可以 reframe：展示为什么 RL-trained selective verification 在 weak agents 上失败—— action-change\n688\t    signal 需要 base agent 足够强才有意义（类比：你不能教一个 25% accuracy 的学生 when to double-check）。\n689\t\n690\t    '\n691\t- name: No-verify ablation\n692\t  plan_id: plan_009\n693\t  description: Episode-level GRPO without self-verification\n694\t  expected_results:\n695\t    val_success: 0.13\n696\t    val_action_is_valid: 0.42\n697\t    always_on_success: 0.25\n698\t    delta_pp: -12\n699\t    avg_trajectory_length: 28.5\n700\t    avg_trajectory_length_with_verify: 41.3\n701\t  result_rationale: 'No-verify 比 always-on 低 12pp，确认 verification 有价值。 但在 worst 档下这个\n702\t    delta 略小于预期的 ≥10pp（12pp 刚过线）， 因为 weak agent 的 verification 质量也不高——agent 经常 verify\n703\t    但 verification 本身也是 noisy。 Action_is_valid 从 55% 降到 42%，说明 verification 确实帮助 format\n704\t    compliance。 Trajectory 更短（28 vs 41 steps）因为没有 verification 步骤。\n705\t\n706\t    '\n707\t  tables:\n708\t  - name: Verification ablation\n709\t    columns:\n710\t    - config\n711\t    - success\n712\t    - action_is_valid\n713\t    - avg_steps\n714\t    - avg_tokens\n715\t    rows:\n716\t    - - always-on verify\n717\t      - 25.0%\n718\t      - 55%\n719\t      - 41.3\n720\t      - 4850\n721\t    - - no verify\n722\t      - 13.0%\n723\t      - 42%\n724\t      - 28.5\n725\t      - 2980\n726\t    - - delta\n727\t      - -12pp\n728\t      - -13pp\n729\t      - '-12.8'\n730\t      - '-1870'\n731\t  figures_description:\n732\t  - 'Paired bar chart: with/without verification across task types.'\n733\t  analysis: 'Verification 有价值（-12pp），但价值不足以支撑 \"selective verification as primary contribution\"。\n734\t    在 analysis paper 中，这是一个 supporting data point：verification matters， 但 training\n735\t    agents to be selective about it requires solving the credit assignment problem\n736\t    first。\n737\t\n738\t    '\n739\t- name: Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\n740\t  plan_id: plan_010\n741\t  description: Stratify action-change-success correlation by policy entropy\n742\t  expected_results:\n743\t    overall_correlation: 0.08\n744\t    overall_p_value: 0.12\n745\t    low_entropy_partial_corr: 0.05\n746\t    low_entropy_p_value: 0.41\n747\t    medium_entropy_partial_corr: 0.09\n748\t    medium_entropy_p_value: 0.18\n749\t    high_entropy_partial_corr: 0.12\n750\t    high_entropy_p_value: 0.09\n751\t    partial_correlation_controlling_entropy: 0.07\n752\t    partial_p_value: 0.15\n753\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：partial correlation 在控制 entropy 后仍不显著（r=0.07, p=0.15）。\n754\t    Action change 与 success 的微弱相关几乎完全由 entropy 解释—— 高 entropy 时更容易 change action（因为\n755\t    policy 本身不确定）， 高 entropy 任务也更可能成功（因为 exploration 更充分）。 控制 entropy 后 action change\n756\t    本身对 success 没有独立贡献。 这直接否定了 \"action change as causal signal for verification quality\"\n757\t    的假设。\n758\t\n759\t    '\n760\t  tables:\n761\t  - name: Entropy-stratified analysis\n762\t    columns:\n763\t    - entropy_stratum\n764\t    - N\n765\t    - action_change_rate\n766\t    - success_rate\n767\t    - corr\n768\t    - p\n769\t    rows:\n770\t    - - low (<0.10)\n771\t      - 768\n772\t      - 11%\n773\t      - 18%\n774\t      - 0.05\n775\t      - 0.41\n776\t    - - medium (0.10-0.20)\n777\t      - 896\n778\t      - 17%\n779\t      - 24%\n780\t      - 0.09\n781\t      - 0.18\n782\t    - - high (>0.20)\n783\t      - 640\n784\t      - 28%\n785\t      - 31%\n786\t      - 0.12\n787\t      - 0.09\n788\t    - - partial (controlling entropy)\n789\t      - 2304\n790\t      - '-'\n791\t      - '-'\n792\t      - 0.07\n793\t      - 0.15\n794\t  figures_description:\n795\t  - '3-panel scatter: action_change vs success within each entropy stratum. No clear\n796\t    trend in any panel.'\n797\t  analysis: 'Action change 不是 independent signal——它是 entropy 的 proxy。 这对 Claim 2 是\n798\t    additional nail in the coffin。Analysis paper framing： \"apparent verification informativeness\n799\t    signals are confounded with policy uncertainty\"， 这是 selective verification failure\n800\t    的又一个 identified mechanism。\n801\t\n802\t    '\n803\t- name: 'Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes'\n804\t  plan_id: plan_011\n805\t  description: 注入 random action changes vs verification-triggered，对比 success\n806\t  expected_results:\n807\t    verification_triggered_success: 0.27\n808\t    random_change_success: 0.21\n809\t    no_change_success: 0.25\n810\t    triggered_vs_random_delta_pp: 6\n811\t    triggered_vs_random_p_value: 0.08\n812\t    triggered_vs_baseline_delta_pp: 2\n813\t    random_vs_baseline_delta_pp: -4\n814\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：verification-triggered changes 仅比 random 好 6pp（p=0.08，边缘不显著）。\n815\t    这弱于预期的 ≥10pp。原因：agent 只有 25% success，verification 质量差， triggered changes 只是 \"slightly\n816\t    better than random\" 而非 \"causally informative\"。 有趣的是 triggered 甚至只比 no-change baseline\n817\t    好 2pp——说明 change 本身（无论来源） 引入了 noise，verification-triggered change 的微弱优势几乎被 change-induced\n818\t    noise 抵消。\n819\t\n820\t    '\n821\t  tables:\n822\t  - name: Causal intervention results\n823\t    columns:\n824\t    - condition\n825\t    - success\n826\t    - N_episodes\n827\t    - 95% CI\n828\t    rows:\n829\t    - - no change (baseline)\n830\t      - 25.0%\n831\t      - 128\n832\t      - '[17.5%, 32.5%]'\n833\t    - - verification-triggered change\n834\t      - 27.0%\n835\t      - 128\n836\t      - '[19.3%, 34.7%]'\n837\t    - - random change (matched rate)\n838\t      - 21.0%\n839\t      - 128\n840\t      - '[13.9%, 28.1%]'\n841\t  figures_description:\n842\t  - 'Bar chart with CI: three conditions. All CIs overlap heavily.'\n843\t  analysis: 'Causal evidence for verification-triggered > random is weak (p=0.08)。\n844\t    CIs 大量重叠，no significant difference。这进一步 disqualifies action-change as reward signal。\n845\t\n846\t    '\n847\t- name: Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\n848\t  plan_id: plan_012\n849\t  description: 对比 action-change / random / confidence-based reward\n850\t  expected_results:\n851\t    action_change_reward_success: 0.16\n852\t    action_change_reward_verify_rate: 0.88\n853\t    random_reward_success: 0.15\n854\t    random_reward_verify_rate: 0.85\n855\t    confidence_reward_success: 0.19\n856\t    confidence_reward_verify_rate: 0.62\n857\t    all_below_always_on: true\n858\t    best_method: confidence-based\n859\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：所有 reward variants 都比 always-on 差。Action-change reward\n860\t    与 random reward 表现几乎一样（delta < 2pp），证实 action-change 不比 random noise 更好。 Confidence-based\n861\t    reward 稍好因为它利用了 model-intrinsic uncertainty 而非 extrinsic noisy signal。 但即使最好的\n862\t    variant 也比 always-on 低 6pp。 核心问题：base agent 太弱时，所有 selective strategies 都退化为 \"less\n863\t    verification = worse performance\"。\n864\t\n865\t    '\n866\t  tables:\n867\t  - name: Reward ablation\n868\t    columns:\n869\t    - reward_type\n870\t    - success\n871\t    - verify_rate\n872\t    - token_cost\n873\t    rows:\n874\t    - - always-on (no skip)\n875\t      - 25.0%\n876\t      - 100%\n877\t      - 1.0x\n878\t    - - action-change\n879\t      - 16.0%\n880\t      - 88%\n881\t      - 0.93x\n882\t    - - random trigger\n883\t      - 15.0%\n884\t      - 85%\n885\t      - 0.90x\n886\t    - - confidence-based\n887\t      - 19.0%\n888\t      - 62%\n889\t      - 0.72x\n890\t  figures_description:\n891\t  - 'Cost-performance Pareto: confidence-based is on frontier, action-change and random\n892\t    are dominated.'\n893\t  analysis: 'Action-change reward 无法区分于 random——这是对 Claim 2 的最终否定。 全部移入 future work：\"selective\n894\t    verification requires (1) stronger base agent, (2) better reward signal\"。\n895\t\n896\t    '\n897\t- name: ARES reproduction + comparison\n898\t  plan_id: plan_013\n899\t  description: 复现 ARES SFT router，与 B-IAVR 对比\n900\t  expected_results:\n901\t    ares_success: 0.22\n902\t    ares_verify_rate: 0.7\n903\t    ares_cost_reduction: 0.3\n904\t    biavr_success: 0.16\n905\t    biavr_verify_rate: 0.88\n906\t    biavr_cost_reduction: 0.12\n907\t    ares_dominates_biavr: true\n908\t    delta_success_pp: 6\n909\t    delta_cost_reduction_pp: 18\n910\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：ARES SFT router 优于 B-IAVR。SFT router 使用 supervised learning\n911\t    from oracle labels（何时 verify 有帮助），不依赖 RL training signal quality。 因此 ARES 不受 action-change\n912\t    noise 影响。B-IAVR 的 RL-trained policy 在 weak reward signal 下退化为 near-always-verify，丧失了\n913\t    cost reduction 优势。 这进一步证明在 weak agent 设定下 SFT > RL for selective verification。\n914\t\n915\t    '\n916\t  tables:\n917\t  - name: ARES vs B-IAVR\n918\t    columns:\n919\t    - method\n920\t    - success\n921\t    - verify_rate\n922\t    - cost_red\n923\t    - dominates\n924\t    rows:\n925\t    - - ARES (SFT)\n926\t      - 22.0%\n927\t      - 70%\n928\t      - 30%\n929\t      - 'yes'\n930\t    - - B-IAVR (RL)\n931\t      - 16.0%\n932\t      - 88%\n933\t      - 12%\n934\t      - 'no'\n935\t  figures_description:\n936\t  - Pareto plot with ARES and B-IAVR. ARES clearly dominates.\n937\t  analysis: 'ARES domination 在 worst 档下是 expected——SFT with oracle labels 是 easier\n938\t    optimization problem。 Analysis paper 可以 acknowledge this 并 discuss when RL might\n939\t    outperform SFT (hypothetically: when base agent is strong enough for action-change\n940\t    to be meaningful signal)。\n941\t\n942\t    '\n943\t- name: ScienceWorld transfer\n944\t  plan_id: plan_014\n945\t  description: ScienceWorld 上验证 episode-level vs step-independent\n946\t  expected_results:\n947\t    episode_level_success: 0.15\n948\t    step_independent_success: 0.03\n949\t    ratio: 5.0\n950\t    episode_level_std: 0.08\n951\t    step_independent_std: 0.02\n952\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 episode-level 仍优于 step-independent（5x），但绝对数值低。 ScienceWorld\n953\t    任务更长更复杂（平均 40+ steps），episode-level 的 bandit credit 更吃力。 但 step-independent 在\n954\t    ScienceWorld 上也崩溃（3%），证明问题不是 ALFWorld-specific。 这支持 analysis paper 的 generalizability\n955\t    claim，但低绝对值（15%）进一步证明 episode-level 不够——需要 finer credit。High std (8pp) 说明 instability\n956\t    也泛化。\n957\t\n958\t    '\n959\t  tables:\n960\t  - name: ScienceWorld transfer\n961\t    columns:\n962\t    - method\n963\t    - success\n964\t    - std\n965\t    - vs_step_independent\n966\t    rows:\n967\t    - - step-independent\n968\t      - 3%\n969\t      - 2pp\n970\t      - baseline\n971\t    - - episode-level\n972\t      - 15%\n973\t      - 8pp\n974\t      - 5x\n975\t  figures_description:\n976\t  - 'Cross-environment comparison: ALFWorld + ScienceWorld paired bars. Same trend\n977\t    (episode > step-ind) but lower absolute for ScienceWorld.'\n978\t  analysis: 'Transfer 验证了 finding 的 generalizability。两个环境一致：episode-level 解决了 step-independent\n979\t    的崩溃， 但自身也有 ceiling。ScienceWorld 的 lower ceiling（15% vs 25%）反映更长 horizon 的 credit\n980\t    challenge。\n981\t\n982\t    '\n983\t- name: 7B model scaling verification\n984\t  plan_id: plan_015\n985\t  description: Qwen3-7B 上验证 episode-level vs step-independent\n986\t  expected_results:\n987\t    episode_level_7b_success: 0.32\n988\t    step_independent_7b_success: 0.08\n989\t    episode_level_1_7b_success: 0.25\n990\t    step_independent_1_7b_success: 0.01\n991\t    scaling_gain_episode_pp: 7\n992\t    scaling_gain_step_ind_pp: 7\n993\t    ratio_7b: 4.0\n994\t    ratio_1_7b: 25.0\n995\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：7B 提升两种方法各约 7pp（近乎 parallel shift），episode-level 优势 ratio\n996\t    缩小（4x vs 25x at 1.7B）。 Step-independent 在 7B 上不再完全崩溃（8% vs 1%），因为 larger model\n997\t    有更好的 in-context learning 能力， 部分补偿了 credit assignment 问题。但 episode-level 仍然 superior。\n998\t    对 paper 的含义：episode-level 优势在 larger model 上缩小——可能 scaling 本身 partially mitigates\n999\t    credit assignment failures（模型 in-context 能力可以补偿 training signal noise）。 这是 analysis\n1000\t    paper 的一个 nuanced finding。\n1001\t\n1002\t    '\n1003\t  tables:\n1004\t  - name: Scaling comparison\n1005\t    columns:\n1006\t    - model\n1007\t    - episode-level\n1008\t    - step-independent\n1009\t    - ratio\n1010\t    rows:\n1011\t    - - Qwen3-1.7B\n1012\t      - 25%\n1013\t      - 1%\n1014\t      - 25x\n1015\t    - - Qwen3-7B\n1016\t      - 32%\n1017\t      - 8%\n1018\t      - 4x\n1019\t  figures_description:\n1020\t  - '2×2 bar chart: model × method. Episode-level advantage shrinks at scale but persists.'\n1021\t  analysis: 'Scaling 结果 nuances the story：credit assignment 问题 severity 与 model size\n1022\t    负相关， 但不消失。Analysis paper 可以 speculate：at sufficient scale（70B+）， in-context learning\n1023\t    可能完全 compensate——这是 \"why big-lab RL works but small-model RL fails\" 的一个 hypothesis。\n1024\t\n1025\t    '\n1026\t- name: Per-task-type breakdown analysis\n1027\t  plan_id: plan_016\n1028\t  description: 按 ALFWorld 任务类型 breakdown episode-level performance\n1029\t  expected_results:\n1030\t    pick_success: 0.35\n1031\t    clean_success: 0.22\n1032\t    heat_success: 0.2\n1033\t    cool_success: 0.18\n1034\t    examine_success: 0.3\n1035\t    pick_two_success: 0.1\n1036\t    episode_length_correlation: 0.48\n1037\t    task_complexity_correlation: -0.62\n1038\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下，simple tasks（pick: 35%, examine: 30%）显著优于 complex tasks（pick_two:\n1039\t    10%, cool: 18%）。 Task complexity-success correlation = -0.62：越复杂越差，符合 credit assignment\n1040\t    bottleneck 假说—— longer horizons = more steps sharing same advantage = coarser\n1041\t    credit = worse learning。 Pick_two 最差因为需要 two sequential subtask completions，episode-level\n1042\t    advantage 无法 区分第一个 pick 的 credit 和第二个 pick 的 credit。 这个 breakdown 对 analysis paper\n1043\t    有价值：展示 failure 不均匀， task structure（horizon length、subtask decomposition）直接影响 credit\n1044\t    assignment quality。\n1045\t\n1046\t    '\n1047\t  tables:\n1048\t  - name: Per-task breakdown (episode-level, 5-seed mean)\n1049\t    columns:\n1050\t    - task_type\n1051\t    - success\n1052\t    - std\n1053\t    - avg_steps\n1054\t    - n_subtasks\n1055\t    rows:\n1056\t    - - pick\n1057\t      - 35%\n1058\t      - 5pp\n1059\t      - 28\n1060\t      - 1\n1061\t    - - examine\n1062\t      - 30%\n1063\t      - 6pp\n1064\t      - 32\n1065\t      - 1\n1066\t    - - clean\n1067\t      - 22%\n1068\t      - 7pp\n1069\t      - 35\n1070\t      - 2\n1071\t    - - heat\n1072\t      - 20%\n1073\t      - 8pp\n1074\t      - 37\n1075\t      - 2\n1076\t    - - cool\n1077\t      - 18%\n1078\t      - 7pp\n1079\t      - 38\n1080\t      - 2\n1081\t    - - pick_two\n1082\t      - 10%\n1083\t      - 9pp\n1084\t      - 45\n1085\t      - 2\n1086\t  figures_description:\n1087\t  - Grouped bar chart by task type, sorted by complexity. Clear downward trend.\n1088\t  - 'Scatter: avg_episode_length vs success per task type, r=-0.62.'\n1089\t  analysis: Task-level breakdown 是 analysis paper 的 key supporting evidence： credit\n1090\t    assignment failure severity 与 task horizon 和 subtask decomposition 正相关。 pick_two\n1091\t    的 10% 证明 episode-level bandit credit 无法处理 multi-subtask credit separation。 这 motivates\n1092\t    future work on hierarchical credit assignment（per-subtask reward 或 option-level\n1093\t    advantage）。\n1094\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa92117-dd67-43a6-a8f9-8378acfec5f6","uuid":"c61d0040-e249-4e5d-941b-f954869cfd90","timestamp":"2026-05-17T12:54:14.136Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T121256/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '完全 reframe 为 diagnostic/analysis paper。Title: \"Dissecting Credit\n  Assignment Failure in Multi-Turn LLM Agent RL: A Dual-Mechanism Analysis\"。 核心叙事：episode-level\n  是 necessary but not sufficient，消除 window-level 问题后暴露更深层 credit assignment 瓶颈。 GAE\n  >> episode-level GRPO 证明 per-token credit 是关键缺失。Sign misattribution 是主要但非唯一因素——entropy\n  collapse、KL drift、information loss 共同作用。 贡献定位为 failure mode taxonomy + actionable\n  guidelines + cross-framework design analysis。 Selective verification 完全移入 future\n  work。Claim 2/3 删除。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Episode-level GRPO convergence (exp029 continuation)\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: Episode-level GRPO 继续训练至 step 50+，观察是否突破 28% plateau\n  expected_results:\n    step15_val_success: 0.28125\n    step20_val_success: 0.27\n    step30_val_success: 0.26\n    step40_val_success: 0.25\n    step50_val_success: 0.24\n    convergence_val_success: 0.25\n    step50_train_success: 0.5\n    step50_train_pass_at_8: 0.8125\n    step50_val_pass_at_1: 0.25\n    step50_val_pass_at_8: 0.94\n    step50_val_action_is_valid: 0.58\n    step50_entropy: 0.12\n    step50_ppo_kl: 0.015\n    train_val_gap_pp: 25\n    plateau_onset_step: 10\n    plateau_duration_steps: 40\n  result_rationale: 'Episode-level GRPO 在 step 10 后进入 plateau（25-28%），训练 success 持续上升至\n    ~50% 但 val 不跟随—— 经典 overfitting to training distribution。根因：GRPO 的 bandit-style\n    credit assignment（所有 token 共享同一 advantage） 无法学习 per-step 策略改进。模型学会了 \"在训练任务分布上做对的\n    trajectory pattern\"，但缺乏 fine-grained credit 来泛化到 unseen task instance。Entropy\n    持续下降表明 policy 在 narrowing 但未在 improving。 pass@8=0.94 证明 policy 有能力但 greedy decoding\n    无法稳定触发正确路径——credit assignment 不够精细， 无法可靠地将 probability mass 集中到 correct action\n    sequence 上。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Convergence trajectory\n    columns:\n    - step\n    - val_success\n    - train_success\n    - val_pass@8\n    - entropy\n    - kl\n    rows:\n    - - 5\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.31\n      - 0.88\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.003\n    - - 10\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.17\n      - 0.007\n    - - 15\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.44\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.01\n    - - 20\n      - 0.27\n      - 0.47\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.012\n    - - 30\n      - 0.26\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.94\n      - 0.13\n      - 0.014\n    - - 40\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.94\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.015\n    - - 50\n      - 0.24\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.94\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.015\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Learning curve: val_success plateau at 25-28% from step 10 onward, train_success\n    diverging upward to 50%. Classic overfitting gap.'\n  - 'Entropy decay curve: monotonic decrease from 0.25 → 0.12, policy narrows without\n    improving generalization.'\n  analysis: 'Plateau 确认 episode-level GRPO 的根本限制：bandit-style advantage 足以消除 sign\n    misattribution， 但不足以提供 per-token credit assignment。25-28% 是 \"episode-level 能做到的天花板\"\n    在当前 reward density 下。 这是 analysis paper 的核心发现之一：episode-level 解决了 step-independent\n    的问题但暴露了更深层瓶颈。\n\n    '\n- name: Context window h-sweep ablation (3 seeds each)\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: h={2, 5, 10, 20, full} sweep，每个 3 seeds，15 steps each\n  expected_results:\n    h2_seed1_step15_success: 0.0\n    h2_seed2_step15_success: 0.03\n    h2_seed3_step15_success: 0.0\n    h2_mean: 0.01\n    h2_std: 0.017\n    h2_collapse_step_mean: 4.3\n    h5_seed1_step15_success: 0.06\n    h5_seed2_step15_success: 0.0\n    h5_seed3_step15_success: 0.09\n    h5_mean: 0.05\n    h5_std: 0.046\n    h5_collapse_rate: 0.33\n    h10_seed1_step15_success: 0.12\n    h10_seed2_step15_success: 0.03\n    h10_seed3_step15_success: 0.16\n    h10_mean: 0.103\n    h10_std: 0.066\n    h20_seed1_step15_success: 0.19\n    h20_seed2_step15_success: 0.09\n    h20_seed3_step15_success: 0.22\n    h20_mean: 0.167\n    h20_std: 0.068\n    full_seed1_step15_success: 0.28\n    full_seed2_step15_success: 0.19\n    full_seed3_step15_success: 0.25\n    full_mean: 0.24\n    full_std: 0.046\n    monotonic_ordering_violated: true\n    h5_occasionally_beats_h10: true\n    h20_occasionally_collapses: true\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档的关键特征：h-sweep 不是 clean monotonic function。h=2 一致崩溃（sign\n    misattribution + extreme information loss）， 但 h=5 和 h=10 之间、h=10 和 h=20 之间存在 seed\n    间交叉——某些 seed 下 h=5 偶尔优于 h=10， h=20 偶尔 collapse。这说明 cliff 位置依赖于 random initialization\n    和 early training dynamics， 而非仅由 h 值决定。高 cross-seed variance 削弱了 \"clean cliff at\n    h=10\" 的叙事， 但仍支持 \"smaller h systematically worse on average\" 的趋势。Non-monotonicity\n    来自 不同 seed 的 entropy dynamics 差异：某些 seed 早期 exploration 更好，偶尔让 h=5 找到可行策略。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: h-sweep summary (step 15, 3 seeds)\n    columns:\n    - h\n    - seed1\n    - seed2\n    - seed3\n    - mean\n    - std\n    - collapse_rate\n    rows:\n    - - h=2\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.01\n      - 0.017\n      - 3/3\n    - - h=5\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.046\n      - 1/3\n    - - h=10\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.16\n      - 0.103\n      - 0.066\n      - 0/3\n    - - h=20\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.167\n      - 0.068\n      - 0/3\n    - - full\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.24\n      - 0.046\n      - 0/3\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Box plot: h vs val_success with individual seed points. Trend is upward but boxes\n    overlap between adjacent h values. Error bars large.'\n  - 'Collapse timeline: h=2 collapses by step 4-5 across all seeds; h=5 collapses\n    in 1/3 seeds; h≥10 no full collapse but h=20 seed2 shows temporary dip.'\n  analysis: 'Non-monotonic 结果对 paper 是挑战也是机会。不能 claim \"clean cliff\"，但可以 reframe 为\n    \"credit assignment failure is a stochastic phenomenon whose probability increases\n    with smaller h\"—— 这更符合 analysis paper 的 tone。Cross-seed variance 本身是 failure mode\n    taxonomy 的一条： \"training instability as a function of context window\" 是独立 failure\n    mechanism。 需要从 \"threshold effect\" 叙事转向 \"probabilistic degradation\" 叙事。\n\n    '\n- name: Multi-seed replication (5 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: Episode-level GRPO 5 seeds（含 exp029 原始 seed），report mean ± std\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_val_success: 0.28\n    seed2_val_success: 0.19\n    seed3_val_success: 0.25\n    seed4_val_success: 0.15\n    seed5_val_success: 0.3\n    mean_val_success: 0.234\n    std_val_success: 0.062\n    std_pp: 6.2\n    min_val_success: 0.15\n    max_val_success: 0.3\n    range_pp: 15\n    seeds_above_25pct: 3\n    seeds_below_20pct: 1\n    mean_train_success: 0.46\n    train_val_gap_mean_pp: 22.6\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档要求 std > 7pp。这里 std=6.2pp 接近但略低于 7pp 边界——真实的 worst 场景中\n    5 seeds 可能落在 6-9pp 范围。 关键问题：seed4 只达到 15%（接近 step-independent 水平），说明 episode-level\n    的优势在某些 seed 下大幅削弱。 这源于 GRPO 的 group normalization 对初始 rollout 分布敏感——如果前几步 rollout\n    恰好全部失败， advantage 全为 0（无 variance），模型无法获得有效梯度。Seed4 可能经历了 \"cold start\" 问题： 早期\n    rollout 全败 → advantage=0 → 无学习 → 持续全败的恶性循环。高 variance 使 95% CI 覆盖 0， 削弱了 episode-level\n    作为 \"solution\" 的 claim，但强化了 analysis paper 的叙事—— \"即使 episode-level 也不稳定，RL for\n    LLM agents 需要更根本性的改进\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Multi-seed results (step 15 checkpoint)\n    columns:\n    - seed\n    - val_success\n    - train_success\n    - action_is_valid\n    - plateau_step\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.44\n      - 0.55\n      - 10\n    - - 2\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.41\n      - 0.52\n      - 8\n    - - 3\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.47\n      - 0.56\n      - 10\n    - - 4\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.48\n      - 12\n    - - 5\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.58\n      - 10\n  - name: Summary statistics\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - mean\n    - std\n    - 95% CI\n    rows:\n    - - val_success\n      - 0.234\n      - 0.062\n      - '[0.157, 0.311]'\n    - - train_success\n      - 0.434\n      - 0.057\n      - '[0.363, 0.505]'\n    - - action_is_valid\n      - 0.538\n      - 0.038\n      - '[0.491, 0.585]'\n  figures_description:\n  - Swarm plot with mean ± 95% CI. CI is wide (15.7pp-31.1%), overlaps with step-independent\n    range for low seeds.\n  analysis: '95% CI [15.7%, 31.1%] 太宽，无法 credibly claim episode-level \"solves\" the\n    problem。 但 mean 仍显著高于 step-independent mean（~2%），所以 \"episode-level helps but doesn''t\n    solve\" 是可靠 claim。 Analysis paper framing: 这证明了 credit assignment 问题的多层性——episode-level\n    消除了 sign misattribution 但暴露了 GRPO 的 cold-start sensitivity 和 bandit-level credit\n    的根本限制。\n\n    '\n- name: GAE baseline comparison\n  plan_id: plan_003b\n  description: GAE(λ=0.95) 和 GAE(λ=1.0, γ=1.0) baselines，15 steps × 3 seeds\n  expected_results:\n    gae_095_seed1_success: 0.44\n    gae_095_seed2_success: 0.38\n    gae_095_seed3_success: 0.41\n    gae_095_mean: 0.41\n    gae_095_std: 0.03\n    gae_10_10_seed1_success: 0.37\n    gae_10_10_seed2_success: 0.34\n    gae_10_10_seed3_success: 0.39\n    gae_10_10_mean: 0.367\n    gae_10_10_std: 0.025\n    episode_grpo_mean: 0.234\n    gae_095_vs_episode_delta_pp: 17.6\n    gae_10_vs_episode_delta_pp: 13.3\n    gae_095_per_token_adv_variance: 0.42\n    episode_grpo_per_token_adv_variance: 0.0\n    step_independent_mean: 0.02\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档要求 GAE >> episode-level GRPO（delta > 15pp）。GAE(λ=0.95)\n    达到 41%—— 因为 critic 提供 per-token temporal difference signal，每个 action 获得独立的 advantage\n    estimate， 而非 GRPO 的 \"全 trajectory 同一 advantage\"。这是 worst 档的核心发现： episode-level\n    GRPO 的 plateau 不是 episode-level 本身的问题，而是 GRPO 的 bandit-style credit 的问题。 GAE 通过\n    value function 提供 fine-grained credit，打破了 plateau。 GAE(λ=1,γ=1) 略低于 GAE(0.95)，因为无\n    discount 导致 variance 更高。 Delta=17.6pp 直接证明：per-token credit assignment 是关键缺失，episode-level\n    只是 necessary condition。 这彻底改变 paper story——从 \"episode-level solves it\" 到 \"episode-level\n    is necessary but per-token credit is the real bottleneck\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Method comparison (step 15)\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - seed1\n    - seed2\n    - seed3\n    - mean\n    - std\n    rows:\n    - - step-independent (h=2)\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.01\n      - 0.017\n    - - episode-level GRPO\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.24\n      - 0.046\n    - - GAE(λ=1,γ=1)\n      - 0.37\n      - 0.34\n      - 0.39\n      - 0.367\n      - 0.025\n    - - GAE(λ=0.95,γ=1)\n      - 0.44\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.41\n      - 0.41\n      - 0.03\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: 4 methods with error bars. Clear staircase: step-ind << episode-GRPO\n    << GAE(1,1) < GAE(0.95). Gap between GRPO and GAE is the paper''s key diagnostic\n    finding.'\n  analysis: 'GAE 的大幅领先是 analysis paper 的最强证据：问题不只是 window-level vs episode-level，\n    而是 credit granularity 的 spectrum。GRPO episode-level 在 spectrum 中间（消除了 sign error\n    但无 per-token credit）， GAE 在另一端（full per-token credit via value function）。这支持 failure\n    mode taxonomy 的第三种机制： \"bandit-level credit insufficiency\"——即使 advantage 方向正确，所有\n    token 共享同一 magnitude 也无法 区分 trajectory 中的关键决策点和无关步骤。\n\n    '\n- name: Episode-level + valid_action_bonus\n  plan_id: plan_003c\n  description: Episode-level + valid_action_bonus=0.05，测试是否安全突破 plateau\n  expected_results:\n    step15_val_success: 0.22\n    step15_val_action_is_valid: 0.72\n    step15_train_success: 0.39\n    valid_bonus_vs_task_ratio: 0.35\n    gaming_detected: false\n    success_improvement_vs_baseline: -0.06\n    action_is_valid_improvement_pp: 17\n    reward_composition_valid_pct: 0.28\n    reward_composition_task_pct: 0.72\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 valid_action_bonus 在 episode-level 中不 game（因为模型优化整条\n    trajectory total reward）， action_is_valid 确实从 55% 提升到 72%，但 success 反而略降（22% <\n    28%）。 原因：valid_action_bonus 改变了 reward landscape，使模型偏向 \"safe but ineffective\"\n    actions—— valid 但不 goal-directed 的 action（如反复 examine 已知物体）获得持续正 reward， 而 risky\n    but potentially successful 的 exploration 策略被抑制。Episode-level 下不存在 per-step gaming，\n    但 dense bonus 仍扭曲了 trajectory-level 的 learning signal——模型学会生成 \"很多 valid action\n    的长 trajectory\" 而非 \"goal-directed 的短 trajectory\"。这是 analysis paper 的另一个 insight：\n    dense reward 在 episode-level 下的失效模式与 step-independent 不同但同样有害。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: valid_action_bonus ablation\n    columns:\n    - config\n    - val_success\n    - action_is_valid\n    - avg_trajectory_len\n    - reward_mean\n    rows:\n    - - episode-level (baseline)\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.55\n      - 38.2\n      - 2.81\n    - - episode-level + bonus=0.05\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.72\n      - 45.6\n      - 3.92\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Dual-axis plot: action_is_valid improves (good) but success drops (bad). Trajectory\n    length increases — model generates more valid-but-aimless steps.'\n  analysis: 'valid_action_bonus 未引入 step-independent 式 gaming，但通过 reward shaping 偏移了\n    policy gradient direction。 这是 failure mode taxonomy 的第四种机制：\"reward misalignment\n    under sparse task signal\"—— 当 task reward 稀疏且 episode-level credit 粗糙时，任何 dense\n    auxiliary reward 都容易主导 learning。 进一步证明 per-token credit（如 GAE）才是根本解。\n\n    '\n- name: Credit assignment mechanism empirical verification\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: Per-window advantage logging，验证 sign misattribution 机制\n  expected_results:\n    sign_vs_outcome_correlation: 0.73\n    sign_vs_local_quality_correlation: 0.28\n    magnitude_position_decay_r2: 0.61\n    episode_level_adv_variance: 0.0\n    success_episodes_all_positive_pct: 0.78\n    failure_episodes_all_negative_pct: 0.82\n    mixed_sign_episodes_pct: 0.2\n    gamma_k_decay_slope: -0.032\n    confound_kl_correlation: 0.31\n    confound_entropy_correlation: 0.27\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档的关键：sign-outcome correlation 只有 0.73（而非预期的 >0.95），sign-local_quality\n    correlation 达到 0.28（而非预期的 ~0）。这意味着 sign misattribution 存在但有显著混杂因素。 Correlation\n    < 1.0 的原因：GRPO 的 group normalization 使得同一 group 内的 advantage 不完全由 episode outcome\n    决定—— 如果 group 内所有 episode 都成功（或都失败），normalization 后 advantage 反映 relative 差异而非\n    absolute 成败。 这在成功率较高的 training episodes 中尤为明显。 Local quality correlation = 0.28\n    的原因：window-local action quality 与 episode success 本身存在弱正相关 （好的 local action 确实\n    contribute to success），所以 sign-local 相关性部分反映了 genuine causal path 而非纯 misattribution。这是混杂因素：无法将\n    sign-local 相关性 100% 归因于 misattribution， 因为部分是 legitimate credit signal。 KL divergence\n    和 entropy 也与 advantage sign 相关（r=0.31, 0.27），说明 policy drift 和 exploration dynamics\n    独立影响 advantage distribution。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Mechanism verification (h=2, seed 2, step 5)\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - observed\n    - hypothesis\n    - status\n    rows:\n    - - sign-outcome corr\n      - 0.73\n      - '>0.95'\n      - PARTIAL — significant confounds\n    - - sign-local_quality corr\n      - 0.28\n      - <0.1\n      - FAILED — non-negligible correlation\n    - - magnitude decay R²\n      - 0.61\n      - '>0.85'\n      - PARTIAL — decay exists but noisy\n    - - episode-level adv variance\n      - 0.0\n      - '0.0'\n      - CONFIRMED\n    - - '% success eps all-positive'\n      - 78%\n      - '>95%'\n      - PARTIAL — 22% have mixed signs\n  - name: Confound analysis\n    columns:\n    - confound_variable\n    - correlation_with_adv_sign\n    - p_value\n    rows:\n    - - episode_outcome\n      - 0.73\n      - <0.001\n    - - local_action_quality\n      - 0.28\n      - <0.01\n    - - KL_divergence\n      - 0.31\n      - <0.01\n    - - entropy\n      - 0.27\n      - <0.01\n    - - window_position\n      - -0.18\n      - <0.05\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter: advantage sign vs episode outcome (color=local quality). Not the clean\n    binary separation expected — significant overlap region.'\n  - 'Partial correlation decomposition: pie chart showing episode outcome explains\n    53%, local quality 16%, KL 10%, entropy 8%, unexplained 13%.'\n  analysis: 'Sign misattribution 存在但不是 sole mechanism——这是 worst 档的核心困难。不能 claim \"advantage\n    sign is entirely determined by episode outcome\"。 需要 reframe 为 \"sign misattribution\n    is the dominant but not sole factor in credit assignment failure\"。 混杂因素（KL drift、entropy\n    dynamics）本身成为 failure mode taxonomy 的独立条目。 Partial correlation decomposition 成为\n    analysis paper 的关键贡献：量化每种机制对 credit assignment failure 的贡献占比。\n\n    '\n- name: Action-change statistics from always-on runs\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 从 exp029 checkpoint 收集 action-change 统计\n  expected_results:\n    action_change_rate: 0.18\n    confirmatory_rate: 0.82\n    action_change_success_correlation: 0.08\n    action_change_success_p_value: 0.12\n    per_task_action_change_std: 0.09\n    pick_action_change_rate: 0.12\n    clean_action_change_rate: 0.22\n    heat_action_change_rate: 0.2\n    cool_action_change_rate: 0.15\n    examine_action_change_rate: 0.25\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 action-change-success correlation 仅 0.08 且 p=0.12（不显著）。\n    原因：episode-level model 只有 25% success rate，样本中 successful episodes 太少导致 statistical\n    power 不足。 更根本的问题：在 25% success 的 agent 上，action change 基本是 noise—— model 的 verification\n    输出质量太低，无论是否 change action 都可能是随机的。 Confirmatory rate 82% 符合预期（大部分 verification\n    不改变行为）， 但这也意味着 action change 事件太稀疏（只有 18%），与 success 的 correlation 在统计上不可靠。 这直接阻碍了\n    Phase B：如果 action change 不是 success 的有效 signal， 用它作 intrinsic reward 没有理论基础。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Action-change statistics\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    rows:\n    - - overall action change rate\n      - 18%\n    - - confirmatory rate\n      - 82%\n    - - action_change-success correlation\n      - r=0.08, p=0.12\n    - - N (episodes)\n      - 128\n    - - N (verification events)\n      - 2304\n    - - N (action changes)\n      - 415\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Contingency table heatmap: action_change × episode_success. No clear pattern\n    — action change is roughly equally distributed across success/failure episodes.'\n  analysis: 'Action change 作为 intrinsic reward 缺乏 empirical grounding。在 worst 档下，\n    这个结果直接导致 Claim 2 无法成立——selective verification 失去了 reward signal。 Analysis paper\n    中可以作为 \"why selective verification is hard for weak agents\" 的一个 finding。\n\n    '\n- name: Selective verification implementation\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: Code-only：实现 binary verify/skip decision\n  expected_results:\n    implementation_status: completed\n    code_changes_files: 4\n    gpu_hours: 0\n  result_rationale: '纯代码实现，不依赖实验结果。在 worst 档下仍可完成，但后续使用这个 implementation 的实验效果差。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Implementation 本身无 worst 档问题。但 plan_005 的 weak correlation 预示 plan_007\n    会失败。\n\n    '\n- name: B-IAVR selective verification training\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 用 action-change reward 训练 selective verification policy\n  expected_results:\n    verification_rate_reduction_pct: 12\n    val_success: 0.16\n    baseline_always_on_success: 0.25\n    success_delta_pp: -9\n    training_converged: false\n    reward_signal_informative: false\n    verification_rate: 0.88\n    policy_learned_skip: false\n    training_steps_before_abort: 20\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：selective verification 无法 deliver clear win。两个根因叠加： (1)\n    plan_005 显示 action-change 不是有效 signal（r=0.08, p=0.12），用它做 reward 等于训练 on noise；\n    (2) base agent 只有 25% success，skip verification 直接降低 performance 且模型无法学会 when\n    to skip。 Verification rate 只降了 12%（模型几乎总是 verify），因为 skip 的 penalty（success 下降）远大于\n    action-change reward 的 bonus。Policy 本质上退化为 \"always verify\"—— 因为在 25% success 的\n    agent 上，任何 skip 都有显著 performance cost。 Success 降至 16%（比 baseline 低 9pp），因为即使少量的\n    skip 也损害了 performance。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: B-IAVR results\n    columns:\n    - policy\n    - val_success\n    - verification_rate\n    - cost_reduction\n    rows:\n    - - always-on\n      - 0.25\n      - 100%\n      - 0%\n    - - B-IAVR (learned)\n      - 0.16\n      - 88%\n      - 12%\n    - - random-50%\n      - 0.14\n      - 50%\n      - 50%\n    - - no-verify\n      - 0.13\n      - 0%\n      - 100%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Pareto frontier: success vs cost. B-IAVR barely separates from always-on, nowhere\n    near efficient frontier.'\n  analysis: 'Selective verification 在 worst 档下完全无法作为 paper contribution。 必须移入 future\n    work，framed as \"requires stronger base agent + better reward signal\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Selective verification full comparison\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: Always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence 对比\n  expected_results:\n    always_on_success: 0.25\n    always_on_verify_rate: 1.0\n    biavr_success: 0.16\n    biavr_verify_rate: 0.88\n    no_verify_success: 0.13\n    no_verify_rate: 0.0\n    random_50_success: 0.14\n    random_50_rate: 0.5\n    confidence_success: 0.19\n    confidence_verify_rate: 0.65\n    biavr_dominates_pareto: false\n    best_cost_performance: confidence-threshold\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：B-IAVR 不 dominate Pareto frontier。Confidence-based baseline\n    意外优于 B-IAVR—— 因为 confidence threshold 是 model-intrinsic signal（policy entropy），\n    比 action-change 这个 noisy extrinsic signal 更 informative。 Confidence 方法在 entropy\n    高时 verify（不确定时检查），在 entropy 低时 skip（确定时省略）， 这 naturally 对齐 \"verification is useful\n    when uncertain\"。 B-IAVR 学到的 policy 没有这种 alignment 因为 training signal 太弱。 所有 selective\n    方法都比 always-on 差（delta > 5pp），因为 base agent 太弱—— verification 在 25% agent 上几乎总是有用的（因为\n    agent 经常犯错）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Full comparison (step 15 checkpoint, 128 val episodes)\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - success\n    - verify_rate\n    - total_tokens\n    - success_per_token\n    rows:\n    - - always-on\n      - 25.0%\n      - 100%\n      - 1.0x\n      - '0.250'\n    - - confidence-0.5\n      - 19.0%\n      - 65%\n      - 0.72x\n      - '0.264'\n    - - B-IAVR\n      - 16.0%\n      - 88%\n      - 0.93x\n      - '0.172'\n    - - random-50%\n      - 14.0%\n      - 50%\n      - 0.62x\n      - '0.226'\n    - - no-verify\n      - 13.0%\n      - 0%\n      - 0.45x\n      - '0.289'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Pareto frontier plot: no-verify has best token-efficiency (trivially), confidence-threshold\n    dominates B-IAVR. B-IAVR is dominated — not on the frontier.'\n  analysis: 'B-IAVR 被 confidence baseline dominate，这对 Claim 3 是致命的。 但 analysis paper\n    可以 reframe：展示为什么 RL-trained selective verification 在 weak agents 上失败—— action-change\n    signal 需要 base agent 足够强才有意义（类比：你不能教一个 25% accuracy 的学生 when to double-check）。\n\n    '\n- name: No-verify ablation\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: Episode-level GRPO without self-verification\n  expected_results:\n    val_success: 0.13\n    val_action_is_valid: 0.42\n    always_on_success: 0.25\n    delta_pp: -12\n    avg_trajectory_length: 28.5\n    avg_trajectory_length_with_verify: 41.3\n  result_rationale: 'No-verify 比 always-on 低 12pp，确认 verification 有价值。 但在 worst 档下这个\n    delta 略小于预期的 ≥10pp（12pp 刚过线）， 因为 weak agent 的 verification 质量也不高——agent 经常 verify\n    但 verification 本身也是 noisy。 Action_is_valid 从 55% 降到 42%，说明 verification 确实帮助 format\n    compliance。 Trajectory 更短（28 vs 41 steps）因为没有 verification 步骤。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Verification ablation\n    columns:\n    - config\n    - success\n    - action_is_valid\n    - avg_steps\n    - avg_tokens\n    rows:\n    - - always-on verify\n      - 25.0%\n      - 55%\n      - 41.3\n      - 4850\n    - - no verify\n      - 13.0%\n      - 42%\n      - 28.5\n      - 2980\n    - - delta\n      - -12pp\n      - -13pp\n      - '-12.8'\n      - '-1870'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired bar chart: with/without verification across task types.'\n  analysis: 'Verification 有价值（-12pp），但价值不足以支撑 \"selective verification as primary contribution\"。\n    在 analysis paper 中，这是一个 supporting data point：verification matters， 但 training\n    agents to be selective about it requires solving the credit assignment problem\n    first。\n\n    '\n- name: Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: Stratify action-change-success correlation by policy entropy\n  expected_results:\n    overall_correlation: 0.08\n    overall_p_value: 0.12\n    low_entropy_partial_corr: 0.05\n    low_entropy_p_value: 0.41\n    medium_entropy_partial_corr: 0.09\n    medium_entropy_p_value: 0.18\n    high_entropy_partial_corr: 0.12\n    high_entropy_p_value: 0.09\n    partial_correlation_controlling_entropy: 0.07\n    partial_p_value: 0.15\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：partial correlation 在控制 entropy 后仍不显著（r=0.07, p=0.15）。\n    Action change 与 success 的微弱相关几乎完全由 entropy 解释—— 高 entropy 时更容易 change action（因为\n    policy 本身不确定）， 高 entropy 任务也更可能成功（因为 exploration 更充分）。 控制 entropy 后 action change\n    本身对 success 没有独立贡献。 这直接否定了 \"action change as causal signal for verification quality\"\n    的假设。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Entropy-stratified analysis\n    columns:\n    - entropy_stratum\n    - N\n    - action_change_rate\n    - success_rate\n    - corr\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - low (<0.10)\n      - 768\n      - 11%\n      - 18%\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.41\n    - - medium (0.10-0.20)\n      - 896\n      - 17%\n      - 24%\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.18\n    - - high (>0.20)\n      - 640\n      - 28%\n      - 31%\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.09\n    - - partial (controlling entropy)\n      - 2304\n      - '-'\n      - '-'\n      - 0.07\n      - 0.15\n  figures_description:\n  - '3-panel scatter: action_change vs success within each entropy stratum. No clear\n    trend in any panel.'\n  analysis: 'Action change 不是 independent signal——它是 entropy 的 proxy。 这对 Claim 2 是\n    additional nail in the coffin。Analysis paper framing： \"apparent verification informativeness\n    signals are confounded with policy uncertainty\"， 这是 selective verification failure\n    的又一个 identified mechanism。\n\n    '\n- name: 'Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes'\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 注入 random action changes vs verification-triggered，对比 success\n  expected_results:\n    verification_triggered_success: 0.27\n    random_change_success: 0.21\n    no_change_success: 0.25\n    triggered_vs_random_delta_pp: 6\n    triggered_vs_random_p_value: 0.08\n    triggered_vs_baseline_delta_pp: 2\n    random_vs_baseline_delta_pp: -4\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：verification-triggered changes 仅比 random 好 6pp（p=0.08，边缘不显著）。\n    这弱于预期的 ≥10pp。原因：agent 只有 25% success，verification 质量差， triggered changes 只是 \"slightly\n    better than random\" 而非 \"causally informative\"。 有趣的是 triggered 甚至只比 no-change baseline\n    好 2pp——说明 change 本身（无论来源） 引入了 noise，verification-triggered change 的微弱优势几乎被 change-induced\n    noise 抵消。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Causal intervention results\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - success\n    - N_episodes\n    - 95% CI\n    rows:\n    - - no change (baseline)\n      - 25.0%\n      - 128\n      - '[17.5%, 32.5%]'\n    - - verification-triggered change\n      - 27.0%\n      - 128\n      - '[19.3%, 34.7%]'\n    - - random change (matched rate)\n      - 21.0%\n      - 128\n      - '[13.9%, 28.1%]'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart with CI: three conditions. All CIs overlap heavily.'\n  analysis: 'Causal evidence for verification-triggered > random is weak (p=0.08)。\n    CIs 大量重叠，no significant difference。这进一步 disqualifies action-change as reward signal。\n\n    '\n- name: Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: 对比 action-change / random / confidence-based reward\n  expected_results:\n    action_change_reward_success: 0.16\n    action_change_reward_verify_rate: 0.88\n    random_reward_success: 0.15\n    random_reward_verify_rate: 0.85\n    confidence_reward_success: 0.19\n    confidence_reward_verify_rate: 0.62\n    all_below_always_on: true\n    best_method: confidence-based\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：所有 reward variants 都比 always-on 差。Action-change reward\n    与 random reward 表现几乎一样（delta < 2pp），证实 action-change 不比 random noise 更好。 Confidence-based\n    reward 稍好因为它利用了 model-intrinsic uncertainty 而非 extrinsic noisy signal。 但即使最好的\n    variant 也比 always-on 低 6pp。 核心问题：base agent 太弱时，所有 selective strategies 都退化为 \"less\n    verification = worse performance\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Reward ablation\n    columns:\n    - reward_type\n    - success\n    - verify_rate\n    - token_cost\n    rows:\n    - - always-on (no skip)\n      - 25.0%\n      - 100%\n      - 1.0x\n    - - action-change\n      - 16.0%\n      - 88%\n      - 0.93x\n    - - random trigger\n      - 15.0%\n      - 85%\n      - 0.90x\n    - - confidence-based\n      - 19.0%\n      - 62%\n      - 0.72x\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Cost-performance Pareto: confidence-based is on frontier, action-change and random\n    are dominated.'\n  analysis: 'Action-change reward 无法区分于 random——这是对 Claim 2 的最终否定。 全部移入 future work：\"selective\n    verification requires (1) stronger base agent, (2) better reward signal\"。\n\n    '\n- name: ARES reproduction + comparison\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: 复现 ARES SFT router，与 B-IAVR 对比\n  expected_results:\n    ares_success: 0.22\n    ares_verify_rate: 0.7\n    ares_cost_reduction: 0.3\n    biavr_success: 0.16\n    biavr_verify_rate: 0.88\n    biavr_cost_reduction: 0.12\n    ares_dominates_biavr: true\n    delta_success_pp: 6\n    delta_cost_reduction_pp: 18\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：ARES SFT router 优于 B-IAVR。SFT router 使用 supervised learning\n    from oracle labels（何时 verify 有帮助），不依赖 RL training signal quality。 因此 ARES 不受 action-change\n    noise 影响。B-IAVR 的 RL-trained policy 在 weak reward signal 下退化为 near-always-verify，丧失了\n    cost reduction 优势。 这进一步证明在 weak agent 设定下 SFT > RL for selective verification。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: ARES vs B-IAVR\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - success\n    - verify_rate\n    - cost_red\n    - dominates\n    rows:\n    - - ARES (SFT)\n      - 22.0%\n      - 70%\n      - 30%\n      - 'yes'\n    - - B-IAVR (RL)\n      - 16.0%\n      - 88%\n      - 12%\n      - 'no'\n  figures_description:\n  - Pareto plot with ARES and B-IAVR. ARES clearly dominates.\n  analysis: 'ARES domination 在 worst 档下是 expected——SFT with oracle labels 是 easier\n    optimization problem。 Analysis paper 可以 acknowledge this 并 discuss when RL might\n    outperform SFT (hypothetically: when base agent is strong enough for action-change\n    to be meaningful signal)。\n\n    '\n- name: ScienceWorld transfer\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: ScienceWorld 上验证 episode-level vs step-independent\n  expected_results:\n    episode_level_success: 0.15\n    step_independent_success: 0.03\n    ratio: 5.0\n    episode_level_std: 0.08\n    step_independent_std: 0.02\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 episode-level 仍优于 step-independent（5x），但绝对数值低。 ScienceWorld\n    任务更长更复杂（平均 40+ steps），episode-level 的 bandit credit 更吃力。 但 step-independent 在\n    ScienceWorld 上也崩溃（3%），证明问题不是 ALFWorld-specific。 这支持 analysis paper 的 generalizability\n    claim，但低绝对值（15%）进一步证明 episode-level 不够——需要 finer credit。High std (8pp) 说明 instability\n    也泛化。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: ScienceWorld transfer\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - success\n    - std\n    - vs_step_independent\n    rows:\n    - - step-independent\n      - 3%\n      - 2pp\n      - baseline\n    - - episode-level\n      - 15%\n      - 8pp\n      - 5x\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Cross-environment comparison: ALFWorld + ScienceWorld paired bars. Same trend\n    (episode > step-ind) but lower absolute for ScienceWorld.'\n  analysis: 'Transfer 验证了 finding 的 generalizability。两个环境一致：episode-level 解决了 step-independent\n    的崩溃， 但自身也有 ceiling。ScienceWorld 的 lower ceiling（15% vs 25%）反映更长 horizon 的 credit\n    challenge。\n\n    '\n- name: 7B model scaling verification\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: Qwen3-7B 上验证 episode-level vs step-independent\n  expected_results:\n    episode_level_7b_success: 0.32\n    step_independent_7b_success: 0.08\n    episode_level_1_7b_success: 0.25\n    step_independent_1_7b_success: 0.01\n    scaling_gain_episode_pp: 7\n    scaling_gain_step_ind_pp: 7\n    ratio_7b: 4.0\n    ratio_1_7b: 25.0\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档：7B 提升两种方法各约 7pp（近乎 parallel shift），episode-level 优势 ratio\n    缩小（4x vs 25x at 1.7B）。 Step-independent 在 7B 上不再完全崩溃（8% vs 1%），因为 larger model\n    有更好的 in-context learning 能力， 部分补偿了 credit assignment 问题。但 episode-level 仍然 superior。\n    对 paper 的含义：episode-level 优势在 larger model 上缩小——可能 scaling 本身 partially mitigates\n    credit assignment failures（模型 in-context 能力可以补偿 training signal noise）。 这是 analysis\n    paper 的一个 nuanced finding。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Scaling comparison\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - episode-level\n    - step-independent\n    - ratio\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3-1.7B\n      - 25%\n      - 1%\n      - 25x\n    - - Qwen3-7B\n      - 32%\n      - 8%\n      - 4x\n  figures_description:\n  - '2×2 bar chart: model × method. Episode-level advantage shrinks at scale but persists.'\n  analysis: 'Scaling 结果 nuances the story：credit assignment 问题 severity 与 model size\n    负相关， 但不消失。Analysis paper 可以 speculate：at sufficient scale（70B+）， in-context learning\n    可能完全 compensate——这是 \"why big-lab RL works but small-model RL fails\" 的一个 hypothesis。\n\n    '\n- name: Per-task-type breakdown analysis\n  plan_id: plan_016\n  description: 按 ALFWorld 任务类型 breakdown episode-level performance\n  expected_results:\n    pick_success: 0.35\n    clean_success: 0.22\n    heat_success: 0.2\n    cool_success: 0.18\n    examine_success: 0.3\n    pick_two_success: 0.1\n    episode_length_correlation: 0.48\n    task_complexity_correlation: -0.62\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下，simple tasks（pick: 35%, examine: 30%）显著优于 complex tasks（pick_two:\n    10%, cool: 18%）。 Task complexity-success correlation = -0.62：越复杂越差，符合 credit assignment\n    bottleneck 假说—— longer horizons = more steps sharing same advantage = coarser\n    credit = worse learning。 Pick_two 最差因为需要 two sequential subtask completions，episode-level\n    advantage 无法 区分第一个 pick 的 credit 和第二个 pick 的 credit。 这个 breakdown 对 analysis paper\n    有价值：展示 failure 不均匀， task structure（horizon length、subtask decomposition）直接影响 credit\n    assignment quality。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Per-task breakdown (episode-level, 5-seed mean)\n    columns:\n    - task_type\n    - success\n    - std\n    - avg_steps\n    - n_subtasks\n    rows:\n    - - pick\n      - 35%\n      - 5pp\n      - 28\n      - 1\n    - - examine\n      - 30%\n      - 6pp\n      - 32\n      - 1\n    - - clean\n      - 22%\n      - 7pp\n      - 35\n      - 2\n    - - heat\n      - 20%\n      - 8pp\n      - 37\n      - 2\n    - - cool\n      - 18%\n      - 7pp\n      - 38\n      - 2\n    - - pick_two\n      - 10%\n      - 9pp\n      - 45\n      - 2\n  figures_description:\n  - Grouped bar chart by task type, sorted by complexity. Clear downward trend.\n  - 'Scatter: avg_episode_length vs success per task type, r=-0.62.'\n  analysis: Task-level breakdown 是 analysis paper 的 key supporting evidence： credit\n    assignment failure severity 与 task horizon 和 subtask decomposition 正相关。 pick_two\n    的 10% 证明 episode-level bandit credit 无法处理 multi-subtask credit separation。 这 motivates\n    future work on hierarchical credit assignment（per-subtask reward 或 option-level\n    advantage）。\n","numLines":1094,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1094}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VM6drHB7RkxQAu7npkd7sh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read both the paper PDF and the review context YAML. Let me understand the task:\n\n1. I need to perform a full review using the dream-review-full dispatch template\n2. Two reviewers: R1 (methods + experiments) and R2 (novelty + related work)\n3. Full roundtable: Step 1 independent → Step 2 cross-share → Step 3 converge → Step 4 synthesize\n4. At the end, submit via `submit_dream_review_report`\n\nLet me now dispatch the two reviewers in parallel. Each reviewer needs the full paper content and the review context to do their job. I'll run them as agents.\n\n\nThe paper diagnoses why step-independent training fails for multi-turn LLM agents, but the empirical results are concerning: episode-level GRPO barely improves to ~23.4% with substantial variance, the hyperparameter sweep shows non-monotonic behavior, and the proposed sign misattribution mechanism only partially explains the failure (r=0.73) with significant confounds present.\n\nThe core issue is that episode-level training underperforms step-independent by 17.6 percentage points, and the action-change signal that should drive credit assignment is essentially noise (r=0.08). Selective verification strategies, including the proposed B-IAVR approach, all fail to improve over always-on verification, suggesting the fundamental mechanisms aren't working as theorized.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38056,"cache_read_input_tokens":24216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38056},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa92117-dd67-43a6-a8f9-8378acfec5f6","uuid":"5aba4d51-31b8-4d14-99f5-9f6139c093c3"}
